## Security Audit Results

**Scope**: `api/` (12 files) + `scripts/` (8 files)

---

### Findings

| # | File | Line | Issue | Severity |
|---|------|------|-------|----------|
| 1 | `api/drip-signup.js` | 5 | n8n subdomain hardcoded as `||` fallback | **MEDIUM** |
| 2 | `api/lead-magnet.js` | 13 | n8n subdomain hardcoded as `||` fallback | **MEDIUM** |

Both follow the pattern:
```js
process.env.N8N_DRIP_WEBHOOK || 'https://winfredquekoc.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/...'
```

The subdomain `winfredquekoc.app.n8n.cloud` is a personal infrastructure identifier — exposing it publicly enables webhook enumeration and direct POST spam bypassing Vercel. No other hardcoded literals were found; all other secrets (`TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`, `PORTAL_SECRET`, `RESEND_API_KEY`, etc.) are correctly env-var only.

**Scripts**: All 8 are pure transformation utilities with no credentials or external calls.

---

### Immediate Fix

Remove the `||` fallbacks in both files — if the env var is missing, return a `503` instead:

```js
const webhookUrl = process.env.N8N_DRIP_WEBHOOK;
if (!webhookUrl) return res.status(503).json({ error: 'Webhook not configured' });
```

---

### Pre-commit Hook

Add `.pre-commit-config.yaml` to the repo root:

```yaml
repos:
  - repo: https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks
    rev: v8.18.4
    hooks:
      - id: gitleaks

  - repo: local
    hooks:
      - id: no-hardcoded-fallback-urls
        name: No hardcoded internal webhook URLs as fallbacks
        language: pygrep
        entry: '\|\|\s*[''\"](https?://[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+\.app\.n8n\.cloud|https?://[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+\.ngrok\.io)'
        types: [javascript, ts]

      - id: no-secret-literals
        name: No hardcoded secret literals
        language: pygrep
        entry: '(?i)(password|secret|api_?key|token|private_?key)\s*[:=]\s*[''"`][^''"`$\{][^''"`]{7,}'
        types: [javascript, ts, python, sh]
        exclude: '(test|spec|fixture|mock)'
```

Activate with:
```sh
pip install pre-commit
pre-commit install          # registers the git hook
pre-commit run --all-files  # one-time baseline scan
```

**Gitleaks** covers 200+ known secret patterns (Telegram tokens, Resend keys, AWS, GitHub PATs). The two local hooks add project-specific coverage for n8n fallback URLs and generic assignment literals.

